  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch05-16--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch05-16: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.72" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.718"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Common ancestry is strongly testable, and ancestral striping can be probabilistically reconstructed. Direct evidence for the ancestral phenotype remains incomplete, so the full historical claim is not decisively resolvable." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Infer Equus relationships and reconstruct ancestral coat-pattern states using ancient and modern genomes, preserved pigmentation loci, fossil evidence and extant phenotype coding. A common ancestor with high posterior support for striping supports the claim; independent stripe origins or a confidently unstriped ancestor refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Coat stripes are rarely preserved in fossils.", "Ancient DNA does not reach the deepest Equus common ancestor and pigmentation genotype-phenotype mapping is incomplete." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch05-16--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch05-16--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch05-16--gpt--dataset-3> .
